  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1250 AM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nToday will stay warm and dry before a cold front moves into the area \nTuesday.  A low chance of showers and thunderstorms are expected to \ndevelop across the northern Brush Country Tuesday morning as the \nfront approaches, then spread and increase to a medium to high \nchance across the Coastal Plains and Coastal Bend by Tuesday \nafternoon. Stronger dynamics will remain north, but conditions will \nstill be conducive to some strong to severe thunderstorms.\n\nCooler and drier conditions are expected Wednesday, with highs in \nthe upper 70s to low 80s. Moisture will begin a slow return back \ninto the area Thursday and Thursday night, with a low to medium \nchance of showers returning. We will be able to get a better handle \non timing as we get a little closer in time.",
